                                 presents:

===========================================================================
                        WiLDNeW v0.3 Multilanguage
                          written by WiLD THiNG
===========================================================================
This  is a new questionaire door for new users, it can give some answers or
comments on the questions and you can have your questinairs in ANSI and you
can have different questions for different baud-rates.  Furthermore you can
ask  new  questions on specified answers (you should now say WOW, no ?  na,
maybe   next   time). 

 Now  you  can  have  your  questions in whatever language you want, i have
supplied  with  this  release  an English, Polish and German one, but don't
forget that the user will probably answer in the language he has been asked
if you don't tell him otherwise.

The  filled in questionaires will be saved in the WiLDTools/WiLDNew/answers
directory with the user name as filename.


Config file:
~~~~~~~~~~~~
(doors:WiLDTools//WiLDNeW/WiLDNew.cfg)
Yes here you must declare which languages you want to have, and the names
of the quest files 
eg.: 
==== cut here ====
English quest.eng
Polski quest.pol
Deutsch quest.ger 
==== cut here ====
and whatever you want...

WiLDNew will ask which language the user prefers.

here  are the recognition chars for the quest file, they have to be at the
beginning of every line:

- print out line
? Ask question
§ Ask question which user MUST Answer 
^ Check answer 
+ Call the editor and let the user write you a comment, that 
        comment will be saved in .../answers/username.com
=xxxxx ask user with specified baud rate where xxxxx is the rate
%xxxxx show line only to user calling at xxxxx baud

You can combine the answer checking with a new question:

?Have you ever heard of WiLDTools ?             - ask question
^yes                                            - if entered "yes" then
§Why not ?                                      - user must answer why
?Is there anything you want to tell me ?
^yes
+                                               - if the answer is
                                                  yes - start the
                                                  editor

Look at the example config file to see some possibilities :)


Installation:
~~~~~~~~~~~~~
To  install  on  /X 3.x just run the WNinst script.  Don't forget to assign
doors:    properly. Now add to yer joined.txt ~CC_WNew, and in da first
line only ~ . That's it...

have phun...

